Please handle the case that `rvalue` is an empty string:
```
if (isempty(rvalue)) {
    *s = mfree(*s);
    return 0;
}
```

This test is already done by [address_label_valid](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/src/basic/socket-util.c#L816)

It is not done in [config_parse_hostname](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/src/network/networkd-network.c#L850) for example.

@yuwata Should I add it anyway ?

In general, conf parsers should have the following steps:
1. unset or set the default value when `rvalue` is an empty string. In this case,
```
if (isempty(rvalue)) {
    *s = mfree(*s);
    return 0;
}
```
2. check and parse the input value. In this case,
```
if (!address_label_valid(rvalue)) {
        log_syntax(...);
        return 0;
}
```
3. assign the value. In this case,
```
return free_and_strdup_warn(datap, rvalue);
```
(`datap` is not a good name, please use `label` or so.)
